    "updated_at": "2021-04-25T06:02:48Z",
    "body": "Turns out it is just yet another performance issue with git. Setting a greater `command_timeout` value will resolve this issue.\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/zsh/starship.toml b/zsh/starship.toml\r\nindex cf89b85..2e55b08 100644\r\n--- a/zsh/starship.toml\r\n+++ b/zsh/starship.toml\r\n@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@\r\n add_newline = false\r\n+command_timeout = 1000\r\n \r\n [character]\r\n success_symbol = \"[➜](bold green)\"\r\n```\r\nHowever, this still raises the question that whether git cli brings better performance than git2 (as stated in #2465).\r\nThis is possibly related to #2625.",
