    "body": "Hi @queensferryme, there are a few things going on here but I think this is mostly expected behaviour. Switching to git was mostly done for performance reasons in larger repos but it also gives us a few other benefits. The biggest being that the git command follows the same timeout as all other commands, there is always a bigger repo or the repo is on a HDD or a network mount or using windows directories in WSL so we needed someway to set a time limit so that starship doesn't hang, for in some cases seconds, while trying to get the status of the repo. This is, as you have noticed, configurable so for users who are patient they can increase the timeout and have the same behaviour as before. We also get rid of a whole class of bugs where libgit2 and git disagree on the state of the repo, see #2212 for example, and make easier to debug when things do go wrong. The downside of the switch is it looks like there was a performance regression in repos that have multiple git submodule but I have a feeling that might be because we weren't properly checking submodule with libgit2 but I have not done any investigation to check if that is the case. Hope this helps. ",
